n\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786671674423629001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ccf6d4dc-1d54-4371-9666-51b124bb1761","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4f50-b1f2-78af-4326"}],"description":"## Context\n`test_dc_corpus_has_eligible_units_that_actually_change` invokes Pandoc for 232 eligible prose units but its only contract is existential: at least one eligible unit exists and at least one changes. Current local runtime is 7.887s/232 subprocesses; an exact short-circuit reaches both witnesses in 0.035s/1 subprocess. Forced identity-renderer and no-eligible mutations fail under both forms. This is exact existential evaluation, not corpus sampling, and matches `any(...)` practice in pytest, Django, and CPython. No tracker rejection was found.\n\n## Plan\n- Freeze the existing two existential postconditions and inventory the full-corpus property tests that independently retain corpus-wide conversion coverage.\n- Strengthen the existing test oracle to prove iteration stops after both witnesses exist while still failing when no eligible or no changed unit exists.\n- Implement exact short-circuit evaluation without changing `_render_unit` or product behavior.\n- Run held-out RED→GREEN, defect-seeded mutation, focused corpus tests, repository gates, and paired timing. Back-out is a Gerrit revert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test still fails if the stratum has no eligible units.\n- [ ] The test still fails if every eligible unit renders identically.\n- [ ] The test stops rendering immediately once both existential witnesses have been observed.\n- [ ] Full-corpus idempotence, no-decay, richness, and hardening coverage remain unchanged in their existing tests.\n- [ ] A defect-seeded non-short-circuit mutation returns the held-out oracle to RED.\n- [ ] Paired timing quantifies saved subprocesses and runner time.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, Gerrit LLM-Review +1, and Gerrit Verified +1 pass before merge.\n- [ ] The final ticket comment records RED/GREEN/mutation evidence and measured savings.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py","reason":"Preserve the existential coverage contract while stopping after both witnesses are found."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","performance","ubuntu","test","pandoc"],"ticket_id":"d792-5507-9df0-4a5f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Short-circuit existential Pandoc corpus witness","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c1ab71c1-e7c9-4132-9a3a-4e2578869a0b","0f6637ba-40ae-4506-905a-43d1e15d84c5","ccf6d4dc-1d54-4371-9666-51b124bb1761","f0b04750-5632-41a8-8e54-74c2ccd1e7f3"]},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786676750637693001,"uuid":"b91a802c-07f6-422f-af15-6f8227ca6b58"}